llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,1151,2026-05-06 01:50:26.107,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,0,"ROOT CAUSE: GET /api/v1/contactservice/contacts/account/{accountId} in ts-contacts-service failed with HTTP 403 due to RequestRejectedException. The URL contained a double-encoded ""%25"" string (representing a literal ""%"" character), which was rejected by Spring Security's firewall as a potentially malicious pattern. The failure propagated from ts-contacts-service to ts-gateway-service."
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,1151,2026-05-06 01:50:26.107,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,1,FIX:
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,1151,2026-05-06 01:50:26.107,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,2,"Remove or URL-decode any ""%25"" from the requesting client's URL path or query parameters before sending to ts-contacts-service."
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,1151,2026-05-06 01:50:26.107,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,3,"If legitimate use of literal ""%"" is required, configure `StrictHttpFirewall` in ts-contacts-service to allow encoded percent signs by overriding `allowedUrlPatterns` or setting `setAllowUrlEncodedPercent(true)`."
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,1151,2026-05-06 01:50:26.107,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,4,Validate and sanitize input URLs at the ts-gateway-service layer to prevent double-encoded strings from reaching backend services.
