llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,5141,2026-05-06 10:40:24.099,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,0,"ROOT CAUSE: ts-contacts-service GET /api/v1/contactservice/contacts/account/{accountId} failed with HTTP 403 due to Spring Security's RequestRejectedException. The URL contained ""%25"" (URL-encoded percent sign), which triggered Spring's strict URL validation rejecting the request as a potential malicious pattern."
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,5141,2026-05-06 10:40:24.099,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,1,"FIX: Modify Spring Security firewall configuration in ts-contacts-service to allow percent-encoded characters in URLs. Add `StrictHttpFirewall` bean with `setAllowUrlEncodedPercent(true)` or set `setAllowSemicolon(true)` depending on context. Alternatively, URL-decode the `%25` to `%` before making the request from ts-gateway-service."
