llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,5143,2026-05-06 10:40:38.247,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,0,"ROOT CAUSE: ts-contacts-service GET /api/v1/contactservice/contacts/account/{accountId} failed with HTTP 403 due to org.springframework.security.web.firewall.RequestRejectedException. The URL contained ""%25"" (URL-encoded percent sign) which was rejected by Spring Security's HTTP firewall as a potentially malicious string. The error occurred at ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker, indicating the request was being processed in a thread pool when rejected."
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,5143,2026-05-06 10:40:38.247,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,1,"FIX: Either (1) Configure Spring Security's StrictHttpFirewall to allow percent-encoded characters by adding `StrictHttpFirewall.setAllowUrlEncodedPercent(true)` in the security configuration of ts-contacts-service, or (2) URL-decode the `{accountId}` parameter in ts-gateway-service before forwarding the request to prevent double-encoding."
