llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,6922,2026-05-06 14:59:57.221,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,0,"ROOT CAUSE: `ts-consign-service` fails on INSERT into `consign_record` table because `handle_date` column receives data exceeding its defined column length (Data truncation error). The failure occurs at MySQL JDBC driver layer, not in application logic. This single root cause propagates to 6 other spans due to cascading failures."
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,6922,2026-05-06 14:59:57.221,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,1,FIX:
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,6922,2026-05-06 14:59:57.221,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,2,Increase `handle_date` column size in database schema: `ALTER TABLE consign_record MODIFY COLUMN handle_date VARCHAR(255);` (or appropriate larger size).
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,6922,2026-05-06 14:59:57.221,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,3,"Alternatively, truncate input data in `ts-consign-service` before INSERT to match current column limit."
llm-communication-20260505-225616.log,6922,2026-05-06 14:59:57.221,deepseek-chat,other,,,,,,,,,,,,4,Add input validation to reject oversized `handle_date` values with proper HTTP 400 response instead of allowing DB truncation error.
